# ============================================================
# PRIVATE DATA — never commit to public repo
# ============================================================
# These directories contain personal memories, session transcripts,
# and private project data. They stay local only. The broad pattern
# (no leading slash) is intentional: catches any nested `people/`,
# `projects/`, etc., anywhere in the tree as defense-in-depth.
#
# Two legitimate code locations are exempted below:
#   - palinode/      shipped code (e.g. palinode/migration/ module)
#   - examples/      shipped sample-data demonstrating the format
people/
projects/
decisions/
insights/
daily/
archive/
inbox/
migration/
research/

# Root-level store artifacts. The directory patterns above miss these: they sit
# AT the root of PALINODE_DIR rather than inside a category folder, so nothing
# above matches them.
#   - entity-aliases.yaml is human-curated and names real people and projects
#     by their actual refs — it is the most identifying file in the store.
#   - .audit/ holds mcp-calls.jsonl and retrievals.jsonl: a record of what was
#     searched for, which is memory content by another route.
# Neither normally lives in a code repo at all. These entries exist because
# PALINODE_DIR is configurable, so a misconfigured dir pointing at a checkout
# would otherwise leave them sitting untracked where `git add -A` sweeps them in.
entity-aliases.yaml
.audit/

!palinode/**
!examples/**

# ============================================================
# Derived / Operational
# ============================================================
# Rebuildable from files
.palinode.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Operational logs
logs/

# Watcher/operational state at the root of PALINODE_DIR (pending queue,
# db-size history). Rebuildable, same class as logs/ above.
.palinode/

# Execution prompts (contain infrastructure details)
M1-EXECUTE-PROMPT.md
M1.5-EXECUTE-PROMPT.md
M2-EXECUTE-PROMPT.md
M3-EXECUTE-PROMPT.md
M3.5-EXECUTE-PROMPT.md

# OS
.DS_Store

# Build artifacts
# #295: generic Python build outputs — rebuilt fresh by publish-pypi.yml on
# tag push, so tracking them in git only causes staleness and bloat.
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
plugin/node_modules/
plugin/dist/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.cover
venv/

# Server logs
server.log
nohup.out
.engram.db
.claude/worktrees/

# Launch-posts working draft — local-only, not for git
artifacts/launch-posts.md

# Test-rig deploy-key material (.claude/plans/test-rigs/) — never commit secrets
.claude/plans/test-rigs/group_vars/all.vault.yml
.claude/plans/palinode-test-env/group_vars/all.vault.yml
